{"@context":{"skos":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#","dcterms":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/","@language":{"@container":"@language"}},"@id":"https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0143","@type":"skos:Concept","skos:notation":"dpp-0143","skos:prefLabel":{"eng":"recoverability"},"skos:definition":{"eng":"declared property of an installation binding (concept dpp-0142) stating whether and how the installed child can resume an independent existence, taking one of the values restorable, harvestable, destructive or absorbing"},"skos:scopeNote":{"eng":"Restorable: the child resumes standalone life; harvestable: recovered but altered, continuing with harvested status and parent history (concept dpp-0144); destructive: the child ceases and flows to a material passport through a transformation event (concept dpp-0129); absorbing: identity dissolves into the parent."}}